WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
The final topic we'll cover is infant choking.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:06.000
We know that babies are naturally curious.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.320
They explore the world with their mouths,

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.960
which means if an object fits in their hand,

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.000
it will likely end up in their mouth eventually.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.120
Your first step is to assess the situation.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.799
A very helpful rule to remember

00:00:18.799 --> 00:00:21.680
is that a crying baby is a breathing baby.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.280
If the choking is mild,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.360
you can simply lean the infant forward

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.400
and pat them on the back to help them clear it.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.520
However, if the choking is severe,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.400
meaning the baby is unable to cry or breathe,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.340
you must act immediately using the five and five technique.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.560
For the best stability,

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.560
it is recommended to sit down with your feet

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.279
flat on the floor and your legs in a V shape

00:00:43.279 --> 00:00:45.520
to help support the infant's weight.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.200
Place the infant face down on your forearm,

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.439
using your hand to support their head

00:00:50.439 --> 00:00:53.880
and ensure their head is positioned lower than their chest.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.959
Deliver five firm back thrusts between the shoulder blades

00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:59.240
while keeping the baby tilted downward.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.959
If the object doesn't clear,

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:03.240
flip the baby over onto your other forearm

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.559
and deliver five chest thrusts.

00:01:05.559 --> 00:01:08.199
Continue alternating between five back thrusts

00:01:08.199 --> 00:01:11.680
and five chest thrusts until the object is ejected

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.099
or the baby becomes unresponsive.

00:01:14.099 --> 00:01:16.260
If the infant loses consciousness,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.160
you must transition immediately to CPR.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.839
Important, regardless of age,

00:01:21.839 --> 00:01:24.160
if a choking victim becomes unresponsive,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.080
begin CPR as you learned today.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.120
The only adjustment is every time you open the airway

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.480
to deliver rescue breaths, look inside the mouth.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.959
Only remove the obstruction if you can clearly see it.

00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:39.279
Never perform a blind finger sweep

00:01:39.279 --> 00:01:41.839
as this can accidentally push the object

00:01:41.839 --> 00:01:43.320
deeper into the airway.

